  "description": "QECXUU crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C140 H138 Dy4 F6 N12 O16,8(C2 H3 N1),C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.605-3.932 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.44-112.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ3-OH)2L6(tmhd)4]·CH2Cl2·8CH3CN (HL = 5-(4-fluorobenzylidene)-8-hydroxylquinoline; tmhd = 2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-3,5-heptanedione); anal. C157H164Cl2Dy4F6N20O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
